  "notes": "{卓越|たくえつ} refers to being distinctly superior or excellent, often used to describe exceptional abilities, achievements, or qualities.\n\nWRITING:\n- {卓|たく} (table; eminent, outstanding)\n- {越|えつ} (exceed, surpass)\n\nUSAGE:\n- {卓越|たくえつ}する (to excel, to be preeminent - suru verb)\n- {卓越|たくえつ}した〜 (excellent ~, outstanding ~)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {卓越|たくえつ}した{技術|ぎじゅつ} (excellent technique/skill)\n- {卓越|たくえつ}した{能力|のうりょく} (outstanding ability)\n- {卓越|たくえつ}した{業績|ぎょうせき} (outstanding achievements)\n- {卓越|たくえつ}した{見識|けんしき} (superior insight)\n\nREGISTER:\n- Formal/written style\n- Common in academic, business, and award contexts\n- Often used in recommendations and evaluations\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {傑出|けっしゅつ} (outstanding, distinguished)\n- {秀逸|しゅういつ} (excellent, superb)\n- {優秀|ゆうしゅう} (excellent, superior)\n- {抜群|ばつぐん} (outstanding, preeminent)",
